    "control_completion": "\n\n**Answer:**\nA solar cell, also known as a photovoltaic cell, converts sunlight into electricity through the following process:\n1. **Absorption of Light:** When sunlight hits the solar cell, it is absorbed by a semiconductor material, typically silicon.\n2. **Generation of Electron-Hole Pairs:** The absorbed light energy excites electrons in the silicon, causing them to break free from their atoms and create a flow of electrons (electric current).\n3. **Electric Field:** The solar cell is designed with a built-in electric field that separates the electrons from the holes (missing electrons). This separation of charges creates a voltage.\n4. **Current Flow:** The separated electrons flow through an external circuit, generating electricity.\n\n#### 10. **Question:**\nWhat is the function of a transformer in an AC circuit?\n\n**Answer:**\nA transformer is a device used to transfer electrical energy from one circuit to another through inductively coupled conductors (windings). Its primary functions in an AC circuit include:\n1. **Voltage Transformation:** Transformers can step up (increase) or step down (decrease) the voltage of an AC supply. This is crucial for efficient power transmission over long distances, as higher voltages reduce current and thus minimize power loss due to resistance in the transmission lines.\n2. **Isolation:** Transformers can provide electrical isolation between the primary and secondary circuits, which is",
